    "id": "news-1787044983538-2",
    "title": "GalMudug Releases Grade 8 Exam Results for 2026",
    "original_title": "Galmudug oo Shaacisay Natiijada Imtixaanka Shahaadiga ah ee Fasalka 8-aad",
    "slug": "galmudug-releases-grade-8-exam-results-for-2026",
    "summary": "GalMudug authorities announced the results of the primary school leaving exam, with 7,881 of 8,104 students passing. The results were presented at a ceremony in Dhuusamareeb.",
    "content": "The GalMudug administration has officially released the results of the Grade 8 primary school leaving examination for the 2026 academic year. The announcement was made today during a public ceremony held in Dhuusamareeb, the administrative capital of GalMudug. The results cover students who sat for the exam in schools across the regions under GalMudug's jurisdiction.\n\nAccording to the Ministry of Education, Culture and Higher Education of GalMudug, a total of 8,104 students registered for the examination. This cohort comprised 4,180 males and 3,924 females. The ministry reported that 7,881 students successfully passed the exam, representing a pass rate of approximately 97.2 percent. The authorities did not specify the number of students who failed or the minimum passing score, but the high success rate suggests a generally well-prepared student body.\n\nThe release of these results marks a significant milestone for students in the region, as passing the Grade 8 exam is a prerequisite for transitioning to secondary education. The exam is a standardized assessment that evaluates students' proficiency in core subjects such as mathematics, science, languages, and social studies. This year's results come at a time when the Somali education system is striving to improve quality and access, especially in federal member states like GalMudug.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these results hold particular relevance. Many diaspora families send remittances to support relatives' education in Somalia, and some may plan to bring their children back to the homeland for schooling. The transparency and efficiency with which GalMudug has conducted and released these results provide a degree of reassurance about the standards of education in the region. Furthermore, students who wish to pursue secondary education abroad may need official transcripts and certificates, making the official release of results an important administrative step.\n\nThe ceremony in Dhuusamareeb was attended by education officials, teachers, and some parents, who received the results with optimism. The ministry has encouraged schools to assist students in the next steps of enrollment for secondary education. As GalMudug continues to develop its educational infrastructure, the timely publication of exam results is seen as a positive sign for the region's commitment to fostering learning and human capital.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/18/galmudug-oo-shaacisay-natiijada-imtixaanka-shahaadiga-ah-ee-fasalka-8-aad/",
    "source": "goobjoog.com",
    "source_name": "Goobjoog",
    "original_url": "https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/18/galmudug-oo-shaacisay-natiijada-imtixaanka-shahaadiga-ah-ee-fasalka-8-aad/",
    "country": "Somalia",
